 "knowledge": "",
 "markdown": "## Summary\nChange the page header title from \"Create Equipment Request\" to \"New Request\" by editing the template's `page-title` attribute.\n\n## How it works today\nThe page uses the `oj-sp-general-overview-page` template, whose `page-title` attribute is set to \"Create Equipment Request\". That string is drawn by the template as the page header title.\n\n## What changes\nThe `page-title` text is updated to \"New Request\".\n\n## The change\n- `webApps/vbredwoodapp/flows/customer-portal/pages/project-create-request-page.html` — change the `page-title` attribute value from \"Create Equipment Request\" to \"New Request\".\n\n## After the change\nWhen the person opens the create-request page (via the dashboard or from an agreement), the header at the top will read \"New Request\" instead of \"Create Equipment Request\". Everything else on the page behaves exactly as before.\n\n## Risks\nNone known — `page-title` is a display-only attribute and is not referenced anywhere else.\n\n## How to test\n1. Open the app and navigate to /vp/shell/customer-portal/project-create-request (the Create Equipment Request page).\n2. Confirm the header title now reads \"New Request\".\n3. Confirm the form, Next button, and all fields still work as before.\n\n## Questions\nNone.",
